# IELTS Reading Mock Document Layout

Use this for **every** IELTS Academic Reading mock (Mock Test 1, 2, 3, …), not only Day 1.

## Shell (`PracticeSession`)

When `isReadingMock` (title/category contains Reading + Mock Test + has `passage_html`):

- Canvas: `#f7f8fa`, no colorful glow blobs
- Width: `max-w-4xl`
- Header: uppercase navy title (`READING MOCK TEST N`), Petrosphere • date, light breadcrumb bar
- Do **not** use the frosted skill card / meta chips header

## Paper body (`ReviewerQuizTaker` + `reading-mock-document`)

- Single-column document (never side-by-side passage sticky pane)
- Sticky question number strip: plain text numbers, Review (amber) / Answered (sky) legend
- Interleave **Passage 1 → Qs → Passage 2 → Qs → Passage 3 → Qs**
- Navy headings (`#1e1b4b`), slate body, generous spacing
- Instructions: bold ranges/keywords (`YES`/`NO`/`NOT GIVEN`/`TRUE`/`FALSE`, `A–G`, `14–19`); option lists in bordered boxes
- Each item: statement + `Answer:` small input (paper style)
- Floating progress FAB: portal to `document.body`, `fixed bottom-6 right-6`, yellow ring + %

## Content import

- Source: LearnDash `.wpq` exports
- Convert with `scripts/convert-reading-mock-N.mjs` → `src/db/ielts-reading-mock-N-seed.json`
- Seed with `npm run db:seed:ielts-reading-mock-N`
- Prefer `fill_blank` answers matching the paper (letters/words/Y-N-NG/T-F-NG)
- Wire hub CTA via `practiceTitle: "IELTS Reading — Mock Test N"` in `ielts-academic-materials.ts`

## Do not

- Reintroduce the two-column reading sidebar for academic mocks
- Trap the progress FAB inside `animate-in` / transformed parents without a portal
